@@ -1362,6 +1362,10 @@ statistics on every tick, with two passive teams and no player seats, units,
 buildings or harvesting. Owner/shared states and statistics must match exactly.
 Setting `GLOB2_GROWTH_PLAYER_FREE_OUTPUT` to a JSON output path expands the check
 from two seeds/64 ticks/32² maps to 20 seeds/512 ticks/64² maps across six scenarios.
+`GLOB2_GROWTH_PLAYER_FREE_DELAY` selects a delay from 1–16 (default 8) for this
+test only. Reports include 128-tick checkpoints, proposal outcomes and a diagnostic
+terminal flush: apply the remaining queue without generating new batches. This
+flush is separate from the normal endpoint and is not a production tick sequence.
 The immediate reference calls the retained old growth pass, not the master engine;
 its RNG schedule and seeding rules differ. Heavy checksums join pending work, so
 these runs establish accounting and ecology, not parallel performance.
